### File-level Variables
@baseUrl = https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com
@httpbin = https://httpbin.org
@contentType = application/json

### 1. Simple GET Request (List Resources)
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts HTTP/1.1

### 2. GET with Query Parameters (Multi-line formatting)
GET {{baseUrl}}/comments?postId=1&_limit=5

### 3. POST Request with Static JSON Body
# @name createPost
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "Sample Mock Post",
  "body": "This is a static JSON payload for testing.",
  "userId": 1
}

### 4. Request Chaining (Using data from the previous response)
# Uses the ID returned by 'createPost' above
@createdId = {{createPost.response.body.$.id}}

GET {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{createdId}} HTTP/1.1

### 5. PUT Request (Full Update)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/posts/1 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "id": 1,
  "title": "Updated Post Title",
  "body": "Completely replaced post content.",
  "userId": 1
}

### 6. PATCH Request (Partial Update)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/posts/1 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "Patched Title Only"
}

### 7. DELETE Request
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/posts/1 HTTP/1.1

### 8. Testing Bearer Token Authentication (via httpbin)
GET {{httpbin}}/bearer HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer my-mock-jwt-token-12345


### 9. Testing Basic Authentication (via httpbin)
# REST Client automatically Base64-encodes username:password
GET {{httpbin}}/basic-auth/admin/secret123 HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Basic admin:secret123


### 10. Form URL-Encoded POST Request
POST {{httpbin}}/post HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username=jdoe
&role=developer
&active=true

### 11. Interactive Prompt Variables
# Prompts you for input in VS Code before sending
# @prompt statusCode Enter an HTTP status code to simulate (e.g., 200, 404, 500)
GET {{httpbin}}/status/{{statusCode}} HTTP/1.1
